      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "No, lowering the dose of St. John's wort will not eliminate the interaction risk and could still make your birth control ineffective. This mixture can become dangerous because \"pseudo-saffron\" in St. John's wort induces liver enzymes that break down hormonal contraception too quickly. Relying on partial reduction is unsafe; instead, please consult a healthcare provider to find a medication-safe supplement or adjust your current plan properly.",
